# *** LOCAL USE ONLY ***
# This file is for local development only. Copy it to .env and edit it to suit your local environment
# The .env file is in the .gitignore. DO NOT COMMIT the created .env file to version control

# *** ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES IN A CDP ENVIRONMENT ***
# To add sensitive secrets, use your service’s secrets page on the Core Delivery Platform Portal
# To add environment variables see: https://github.com/DEFRA/cdp-documentation/blob/main/how-to/config.md

# *** USING ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES ***
# See https://prototype-kit.service.gov.uk/docs/tutorials-and-guides or
# https://github.com/alphagov/govuk-prototype-kit for guidance on using environment variables with the prototype kit
# The README.md has details about the environment variables available in the GOV.UK Prototype Kit

# GOV.UK Prototype Kit Environment variables

#PASSWORD=
#PASSWORD_KEYS=

# Add your own environment variables below

# Where the prototype is published. The journey tools page
# (/tools/journeys/<journey>) uses this for its "copy link" buttons.
# Optional: defaults to https://nrf-prototypes.ext-test.cdp.defra.gov.uk
#PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# Figma Personal Access Token (requires Editor access to the NRF Figma file)
# Generate at: Figma → Account Settings → Personal access tokens
#FIGMA_TOKEN=

# Ordnance Survey Data Hub API key (OS Vector Tile API + OS Names API).
# Used by the production-style map in nrf-quote-7 (app/routes/os-base-map.js).
# Optional: without it the map falls back to the keyless Satellite and Streets basemaps.
#OS_API_KEY=

# Optional, quote V7.1 only: production's services, as the frontend uses them.
# The impact assessor (with OS_API_KEY as well) gives the map production's
# Hybrid (the default) and Aerial basemaps, from its APGB aerial_proxy, and
# production's EDP outlines (see app/routes/tileserver-proxy.js). The NRF
# backend checks the boundary against production's EDPs (POST /boundary/check,
# see app/lib/nrf-quote-7-1/hooks.js). Each needs its URL and its key; a URL
# alone is ignored. Without them V7.1 uses the keyless basemaps and the
# prototype's own EDP data, as quote V7 always does.
#IMPACT_ASSESSOR_BASE_URL=
#IMPACT_ASSESSOR_API_KEY=
#NRF_BACKEND_API_URL=
#BACKEND_API_KEY=
